      equipment: 'Table, deck of cards.',
      dealing: 'The entire deck is dealt out face down to the players as evenly as possible. Players keep their cards in a face-down pile and do not look at them.',
    },
    turnFlow: "1. **The Choice**: Each player announces their chosen animal at the start. 2. **Turning**: Starting left of the dealer, each player flips the top card of their face-down pile face-up onto a personal face-up pile. Cards should be flipped AWAY from the player so everyone sees them at once. 3. **The Match**: When any two players' top face-up cards match in rank (e.g., two 8s), the first of those two players to make the OTHER player's animal noise (or shout their animal name) wins the match. 4. **Winning Piles**: The winner of the match takes both face-up piles and places them face-down at the bottom of their draw pile. 5. **Snap Pot (Optional)**: If any non-matching player shouts first, or a player makes a false sound, their face-up pile goes into a center 'Snap Pot'. The first person to identify a match with the Pot wins it.",
